FOUR RETAINED EDITS, commits da098cc62 / 8dfc76694 / a4d6e1511, all in src/game/world/gauntworld.c::fn_8005F0F4.

(1) A SEMANTIC BUG FIX, found by reading the FPR webs rather than the diff. Target holds SIX callee-saved FPRs (bl _savefpr_26, stmw r25,220(r1)); ours held five (_savefpr_27, stmw r25,228). The whole FPR numbering was shifted by one and the extra register was target f28: `fadds f28,f26,f29` at +0x294 puts a+R into a NEW register while f29 keeps the base radius, and at +0x450 the target does `fsubs f27,f27,f29` - it subtracts the BASE radius, not the sum. Our source overwrote R:
-    R = (f32)(a + R);
-    if (f1*f1 + f2*f2 > R*R) ...      if (dist > R) ...      if (fqdist(dist,nv[1]) > R) ...      if (fqdist(nv[0],nv[2]) > R) ...
+    Rsum = (f32)(a + R);              (new `f32 Rsum;` declared after `f32 R;`)
+    ... all four CULLING comparisons take Rsum; `dist -= R;` keeps the base radius ...
real 739 -> 723.

(2) `f32 unused[12];` -> `f32 unused[10];`. The sixth saved FPR adds 8 bytes of save area, so the pad had to give 8 back: frame 304 -> 296 EXACT. real 723 -> 703.

(3) Local-block re-seat, from the slotdiff map plus the target's `addi r6,r1,N`/`addi r7,r1,N` pair:
-    f32 hitpt[3];  f32 norm[3];        (ours r6=168 r7=156, target r6=140 r7=152 - ORDER INVERTED)
+    f32 norm[3];   f32 hitpt[3];
 and a SECOND pad above the vector block, because the target leaves 20 bytes between nv and its f64 conversion temp where we left 4:
     f32 cx, cz;
+    f32 unused2[4];
     f32 nv[3]; f32 mv[3]; f32 norm[3]; f32 hitpt[3];
     f32 f1,f2,f3,f4;
-    f32 unused[10];
+    f32 unused[6];
real 703 -> 471, slotdiff exclusives 9T/9O -> 2T/2O.

(4) THE HOME-COPY LEVER, and the reason this record refutes the standing law. Target: `lha r0,8(r4) / lfs f29,12(r4) / cmpwi r0,0 / mr r29,r0 / bne`; ours coalesced the load straight into the callee-saved home and was one instruction short. The cure is neither block scope nor a second variable - it is letting the GUARD RE-READ THE FIELD the assignment just cached:
     coltype = data->coltype;
     R = data->radius;
-    if (coltype == 0) {
+    if (data->coltype == 0) {
         return -1.0f;
     }
MWCC CSEs the load into a scratch, tests it there, and homes it with a copy - the target's exact shape. real 471 -> 210 and instruction counts became EXACT at 661/661.

VARIANT G, MEASURED AND REJECTED (the same-scope split the block-scope law predicts would fold): `s32 ct; ct = data->coltype; R = data->radius; if (ct == 0) return -1.0f; coltype = ct;`. It does NOT fold here - it produces cmpwi (killing the extsh. that form (4) leaves behind) and multiset 4t -> 2t - but it moves the copy out of the guard block and measures real 214 and fuzzy 98.7867% against form (4)'s real 210 / fuzzy 98.9153%. Rejected on fuzzy at equal instruction counts per the equal-count law. It is the best-known next form for anyone attacking the two remaining respell rows.
